  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/9705203v1</id>
    <title>Large scale simulations of the Zhang sandpile model</title>
    <updated>1997-05-20T17:21:54Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/9705203v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/9705203v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  We consider the non Abelian sandpile model introduced by Y.-C. Zhang on a two-dimensional square lattice. The static and dynamical properties of the model are investigated and compared to the Abelian sandpile model of Bak, Tang and Wiesenfeld. A detailed analysis which takes the finite size effects into account yields that the exponents of the avalanche probability distribution are the same as in the Abelian model.</summary>
    <category term="cond-mat.stat-mech" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>1997-05-20T17:21:54Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>6 pages, 8 figures, accepted for publication Physical Review E</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cond-mat.stat-mech"/>
    <arxiv:journal_ref>Physical Review E 56, 1590 (1997).</arxiv:journal_ref>
    <author>
